  offerDialogue:
    name: Marsh
    sentences:
    - "There\u2019s a residential district on the other side of the waterway. "
    - The people can already reach <b><#E09500>Central Riverside</color></b>, but
      they have to pass through another district first.
    - That makes the trip longer than it needs to be.
    - A crossing here would give them a much more direct connection.
    - "But there\u2019s one more thing to consider. "
    - <b><#E09500>Boats also pass through this waterway</color></b>.
    - <b><#E09500>So whatever you build has to leave enough room for them to pass
      underneath. </color></b>.
    - "This project uses a different kind of bridge from the ones you\u2019ve built
      before."
    - <b><#E09500>It needs to work for both the road above and the waterway below</color></b>.
    - During the test, make sure the vehicle can cross safely and the boat can still
      pass underneath.
    - <b><#E09500>Take a close look at the shape of the new bridge components and
      the space you leave below the roadway</color></b>.
    - "If you\u2019re ready, I can give you the contract"
  continueOfferDialogue:
    name: Marsh
    sentences: []
  reminderDialogue:
    name: Marsh
    sentences:
    - 'This crossing should make the other area easier to reach. '
    - "<b><#E09500>Pay attention to the bridge\u2019s shape and supports while you
      build</color></b>."
  finishedContractDialogue:
    name: Marsh
    sentences:
    - That should make things a lot easier around here.
    - The residents now have a much more direct way to the main road.
    - "That\u2019s a good start for your first project here, {PlayerName}."
    - "I\u2019m sure you\u2019ll probably come across more projects as you explore
      Town River. \r\n"
